G2749.b:
⟪κεῖμαι⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Jeremiah 24:1|Je 24:1⟧ (⁨יעד⁩ hoph.), al.;] used as passive of τίθημι (LS, s.v.), ⟪to be laid⟫, ⟪to lie⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of persons: an infant, ⟦Luke 2:12|Lk 2:12⟧, ⟦Luke 2:16|16⟧; a dead body, ⟦Matthew 28:6|Mt 28:6⟧, ⟦Luke 23:53|Lk 23:53⟧, ⟦John 20:12|Jo 20:12⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of things, ⟪to lie⟫, ⟪be laid⟫ or ⟪set⟫, ⟪stand⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:14|Mt 5:14⟧, ⟦John 2:6|Jo 2:6⟧ ⟦John 19:29|19:29⟧ ⟦John 20:5|20:5-7⟧ ⟦John 21:9|21:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:2|Re 4:2⟧ ⟦Revelation 21:16|21:16⟧; trop., Θεμέλιος, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:11|I Co 3:11⟧; seq. prep. c. acc., πρός, ⟦Matthew 3:10|Mt 3:10⟧, ⟦Luke 3:9|Lk 3:9⟧; εἰς, ⟦Luke 12:19|Lk 12:19⟧; ἐπί, trop., κάλυμμα, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:15|II Co 3:15⟧. Metaph., ὁ κόσμος ἐν τ. πονηριῷ κ., ⟦1 John 5:19|I Jo 5:19⟧; ⟪to be laid down⟫, ⟪appointed⟫: of law, c. dat. pers., ⟦1 Timothy 1:9|I Ti 1:9⟧; seq. εἰς c. acc. (of purpose), ⟦Luke 2:34|Lk 2:34⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:16|Phl 1:16⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:3|I Th 3:3⟧ (cf. ἀνά-, συν-ανά-, ἀντί-, ἀπό-, ἐπί-, κατά-, παρά-, περί-, πρό-κειμαι).†

G2756.b:
⟪κενός⟫, -ή, -όν,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨ריק⁩ and cognate forms;] ⟪empty⟫ (⟦Genesis 37:24|Ge 37:24⟧, ⟦Judges 7:16|Jg 7:16⟧). Metaph.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪empty⟫, ⟪vain⟫: λόγοι, ⟦Ephesians 5:6|Eph 5:6⟧; ἀπάτη, ⟦Colossians 2:8|Col 2:8⟧; κήρυγμα, πίστις, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:14|I Co 15:14⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪vain⟫, ⟪fruitless⟫: ἡ χάρις, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:10|I Co 15:10⟧; κόπος, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:58|I Co 15:58⟧; ἡ εἴσοδος, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:1|I Th 2:1⟧; κενά, ⟦Acts 4:25|Ac 4:25⟧(LXX); εἰς κενόν, ⟪in vain⟫, ⟪to no purpose⟫ (Diod., LXX; cl. διὰ κενῆς), ⟦2 Corinthians 6:1|II Co 6:1⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:2|Ga 2:2⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:16|Phl 2:16⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:5|I Th 3:5⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of persons, ⟪empty-handed⟫: ⟦Mark 12:3|Mk 12:3⟧, ⟦Luke 1:53|Lk 1:53⟧ ⟦Luke 20:10|20:10⟧, ⟦Luke 20:11|11⟧; ⟪vain⟫, ⟦James 2:20|Ja 2:20⟧.†
SYN.: μάταιος, of the aim or effect of an action, κ. of its quality (Lft. on Cl. Rom., I Co., § 7; Tr., Syn., xlix).

G2799.b:
⟪κλαίω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨בּכה⁩;] of any loud expression of pain or sorrow, esp. for the dead, ⟪to weep⟫, ⟪lament⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ intrans.: ⟦Mark 5:38|Mk 5:38⟧, ⟦Mark 5:39|39⟧ ⟦Mark 14:72|14:72⟧ (M, Pr., 131) ⟦Mark 16:10|Mk 16:[10]⟧, ⟦Luke 7:13|Lk 7:13⟧, ⟦Luke 7:32|32⟧, ⟦Luke 7:38|38⟧ ⟦Luke 8:52|8:52⟧, ⟦John 11:31|Jo 11:31⟧, ⟦John 11:33|33⟧ ⟦John 16:20|16:20⟧ ⟦John 20:11|20:11⟧, ⟦John 20:13|13⟧, ⟦John 20:15|15⟧ ⟦Acts 9:39|Ac 9:39⟧ ⟦Acts 21:13|21:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:30|I Co 7:30⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:18|Phl 3:18⟧, ⟦James 4:9|Ja 4:9⟧ ⟦James 5:1|5:1⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:5|Re 5:5⟧ ⟦Revelation 18:15|18:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:19|19⟧; πολύ, ⟦Revelation 5:4|Re 5:4⟧; πολλά, ⟦Acts 8:24|Ac 8:24⟧ (WH, mg.); πικρῶς, ⟦Matthew 26:75|Mt 26:75⟧, ⟦Luke 22:62|Lk 22:62⟧; opp. to γελάω, ⟦Luke 6:21|Lk 6:21⟧, ⟦Luke 6:25|25⟧; χαίρω, ⟦Romans 12:15|Ro 12:15⟧; seq. ἐπί, c. acc., ⟦Luke 19:41|Lk 19:41⟧ ⟦Luke 23:28|23:28⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:9|Re 18:9⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ trans., c. acc. pers., ⟪to weep⟫ or ⟪lament for⟫, ⟪bewail⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:18|Mt 2:18⟧.†
SYN.: v.s. δακρύω.
